{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of BO1 source readiness at head e272eb7c60fc1f2d70341371d0c08aaa5f732f28, tree c97a1acf, for child request 4c5c41d3 and review request a572e5a1. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nThe head adds eight commits to main 5dc9765f and changes 107 paths. I read the implementation note first, then the diff of the supporting paths, against section 7 of `docs/kernel.md` and rulings 7a2beda6, 33f95e72, d0523c9f and e611ae0e. Two independent reads ran beside mine: one of the kernel and the scope versions, and one of the client, MCP, Page and Worker configuration. I confirmed each finding below in the code.\n\nThe kernel addition is sound. A `reference` is closed and bounded, it creates no FactUse and grants nothing, every older pin keeps its bytes, and the versions can't be mixed across families. The requirement travels from install through Rules14 to Directory22 without a gap. I found no widening of authority and no script injection.\n\nThe defects are elsewhere. A Commons room can't publish to its own Destination, one note can break the Commons screen for every reader, the client discards evidence of a rolled-back head, and the W1 driver follows redirects.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. A Commons room can't publish to its Destination.\n   - The family reuses `destination@16`. That pin's publication check is `unpublishedApplicationPublicationOrigin` (`publishing-provenance.ts:245-246`), which compares exact pins for `directory@20` and `rules@10`. The head doesn't change that file.\n   - `delivery.ts:201-205` selects the check for `destination@16`, and a false answer returns `source-unverified`.\n   - Scenario: a package in a Register23 room needs the Destination, and its lane sends a file publication. The Directory's genesis seed is `directory@22`, so `office.seed.definition !== pins.directory` and the delivery is refused on every retry.\n   - No test reaches this path. `commons-install.test.ts` asserts `destination: false`, and neither the Commons tests nor the bill witness publish. A room that can't publish fails the cohort's stated purpose, which keeps Destination16 for repository rooms.\n   - Fix: accept the Commons pins for `destination@16`, and keep the older family's check exact for older rooms. Add a native case that publishes from a Commons room. If the builder believes that Commons rooms should not publish yet, the question goes to the planner.\n\n2. Any note writer can break the Commons screen for every reader.\n   - `apps/room/page/src/commons.ts:49` reads `values[column]` for columns that come from other rows. `cell` then canonicalizes what it finds.\n   - Scenario: a member posts `{\"toString\":1}` as `application/json` while any other JSON object note is in the window. For the other row, `values[\"toString\"]` is the inherited function, `canonicalize` throws, and the whole screen fails, including the note form. `constructor` does the same. The failure lasts while the note stays in the window. Every role holds `commons.write`, so this needs no special rights.\n   - The independent read reproduced this with a stub DOM.\n   - Fix: read a column only with `Object.hasOwn`. Add a case in `view.test.ts`.\n\n3. The client accepts a rolled-back head as complete.\n   - `loadCommons` uses the summary only for identity, then replaces its head with the history read's head (`packages/client/src/commons.ts:60-68`). It never compares them.\n   - Scenario: a reply gives a summary at head 5, then a history that closes correctly at head 0. The result is `complete: true` at head 0, with nothing marked unreadable. The independent read reproduced this with a fake handle.\n   - A server that lies the same way in both reads stays undetectable. This case discards evidence the client already holds, and the note claims that the client checks the selected head.\n   - Fix: require the history head to be at or past the summary's head, with an equal hash at an equal sequence. Otherwise mark the window unreadable. Add a case.\n\n4. The W1 driver's same-origin bound doesn't hold across a redirect.\n   - The origin check at `examples/commons-bill/witness.ts:191` sees only the first URL. Neither the driver's fetch nor `packages/client/src/http.ts` sets `redirect: \"error\"`, so the default follows redirects, and `witness.test.mjs` has no redirect case.\n   - Scenario: the service answers `POST /acts` with a 307 to another origin. The signed envelope and its detached body go there, the foreign reply counts as the answer, and the hop escapes the 128-request count.\n   - The note states the same-origin bound as a property of the driver.\n   - Fix: set `redirect: \"error\"` in the driver's fetch and refuse a redirected response. Add a case.\n\n5. A host-none Commons room gets the wrong site answer.\n   - `site/host.ts:140` recognizes a room with no repository only for `UNPUBLISHED_COHORT.directory`. `creation-admission.ts` admits host none for `COMMONS_COHORT.register` too.\n   - For a `directory@22` room, `roomOf` returns null, and `route.ts:285` answers `not-found` where the matching older room answers `no-repository`.\n   - Fix: recognize the Commons Directory there, with a case.\n\n6. The kernel-gate text doesn't name all of the additions.\n   - The section gives good reasons for the scope kind, the platform name and the field type. It doesn't name the `ReferenceValue` export (`contract/definition.ts`), the `isReference` export (`bytes/field-value.ts`), or `platform:membership@9` in `INVITATION_KEY_MEMBERSHIPS` (`contract/invitation.ts:7`).\n   - The hold@2 entry in the same section sets the form: name each export, with a reason.\n   - Fix: name them.\n\nItems 1 to 5 change production source or its tests, so a new full gate must run at the final head. All five failed gates stay failed, and gate 6 stays a pass for its source.\n\n## Against the rulings\n\n1. Reference shape. Resolved.\n   - `isReference` needs exactly one of `document` or `entry` and allows no other key except `fragment`. The fragment bound is in UTF-8 bytes, and lone surrogates are refused. `FactRef` stays closed.\n   - `factsNamed` selects only `fact` fields, so a reference makes no FactUse. It isn't assignable to `fact`. No rule, guard or fold of `commons@1` reads `about`.\n   - The size charge is sound: 64 references with 512-byte fragments come to 217,154 bytes, under the entry limit.\n2. Older pins. Resolved. `native-declarations.generated` only adds rows. Every changed recognizer adds an exact comparison for a new pin, and `SIBLINGS_OF` lookups compare with the room's own Directory.\n3. Membership9. Resolved. Its data and rules match Membership8, except that `commons.write` joins all five role lists, and a test compares the lists with `@8` plus that one action. `ownStanding`, session issue and the invitation limiter add only the exact `@9`, and no check is skipped.\n4. Rules14 and Directory22. Resolved. Rules14 stores three required booleans and sends `needsCommons`, and `has-commons` holds when the field is false or the ref is present. All four combinations are tested. The Archive guard is unchanged, and older Rules refuse as the ruling says.\n5. Creation. Resolved. The send is on `establish`, the seed is deterministic so one Directory yields one Commons, and `creation-lineage` admits `commons` only for a cohort that has one, under the exact parent and pin. A register pin selects its family exactly.\n6. `commons@1`. Resolved. It has no guards, sends, operations or code rules. `note` has no effects.\n7. Catalog. Resolved. The count is 85 in `docs/kernel.md`.\n8. W1 and the Worker. Resolved apart from item 4.\n   - The local native witness admits all 23 notes with a real person and a controlled agent, distinct keys and verified signatures. It proves no hosted run, and the note says so.\n   - The `dap-commons` configuration differs from Demo only as expected. It has its own Durable Object classes, and `unplanned` fails closed, so creation is refused.\n9. Rendering and authorship. Resolved apart from item 2. The Page builds no markup from note text, and each note-derived link is `#/commons/` plus `encodeURIComponent`. The signer comes from the entry, and a label applies only when its handle matches the native author in that membership.\n\n## The gates\n\n- Gates 1 to 5 stay failed, each with its row in the note: gates 1 and 2 at typecheck, gate 3 in Node, gate 4 in Plain and gate 5 in Native.\n- Gate 6 at 348ea394, tree 4972b81a, passes all five stages. Receipt ce795b7e exits 0 with complete capture, the same head and tree before and after, and no dropped bytes. Node passes 83 cases, Counting 56, Plain 3,170 with one skip and Native 867 with two skips.\n- From 348ea394 to the head, only the note and the manifest change.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5dc9765f gives the head tree c97a1acf.\n- The 107 artifacts name exactly the 107 changed paths, all at this head. The note was filed last, so the commitment's report is the note.\n- I ran the owning files once each, with no whole suite:\n  - `forms-reference`, `client/commons` and `mcp/commons`: 10 of 10;\n  - native `commons`, `commons-install` and `commons-bill`: 7 of 7;\n  - `examples/commons-bill/test/witness.test.mjs`: 3 of 3;\n  - `security-entry-points.test.mjs`: 10 of 10.\n  - The builder worktree stayed clean.\n- `node scripts/check-kernel-boundary.mjs` checks 126 production sources with no refusals.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 5e40bdf9. All 607 cited files match by size and SHA-256. The directory has 1,474 files and 189,359,526 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` has digest 1a033482 and reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 771 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 5dc9765f: one warning, on the manifest's 113,534 bytes.\n- check-commit-messages from 5dc9765f: 8 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. For the planner: a `reference` field has no format gate. Declared definitions stay `artroom-definition-1`, so a package with a `reference` field now validates in any room, including one on Rules10. Old code refuses it, and I infer no replay divergence, because the case I checked records no refused install. Whether \"older pins keep their meanings\" covers this needs a ruling.\n2. `host.requires` order isn't canonical: `[\"archive\",\"commons\"]` and the reverse both validate, which gives two semantic digests for one meaning. `profiles` must be ordered. Requiring an order is a one-line change.\n3. A package can hold a reference in a fixed slot, where `fixed-index.ts` walks values by shape and records the nested `entry` as a local dependency. This grants nothing and doesn't touch `commons@1`, but \"no index reads it\" holds for Commons, not for every package.\n4. A Commons has no per-member limit. Every role writes, and only the scope budgets bound it. By arithmetic, about 3,800 maximum-size notes would exhaust a scope, and I infer no archive relief. This fails closed.\n5. Hosted MCP's `commons` tool directs callers to `step` and `text`, which `HOSTED_TOOL_OMISSIONS` removes, so a hosted caller can't read complete text. W1 may need that.\n6. Witness gaps: no positive case at 64 references of 512 bytes, and no lineage negative for `commons`.\n7. `notesAbout` took 5.2 seconds in Node on a worst case of 400 notes with 64 references each, and it runs synchronously on each selected view.\n8. `commonsInstallCheck` tests only the ref's shape and kind, where `docs/mcp.md` says \"verified\". Directory22's recorded guard is the real check. `--cohort commons --register-policy open` is accepted for every host, so \"open creation stays off\" rests on configuration.\n9. `docs/deploy.md` tells the planner to maintain `DEMO_START_CONFIG` for Commons, but `demoCreationConfig` requires Register17, so the setting has no effect. `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md` has no `dap-commons` section. `demo-config.test.ts` doesn't pin the Commons configuration. `scope-index-applications.ts` and `scope-index-manifest.ts` omit the new versions, and the manifest's omission fails closed.\n10. The manifest is 113,534 bytes because it cites 607 files. The form follows ruling 4e199bd8. Citing the retained runner units once each would shrink it and clear the warning.\n11. The note's prose relies on shorthand: \"Root\", and run-together forms such as \"closes1/1\" and \"Node83\".\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe kernel holds only what runtime and replay must agree on, and the host owns media, threads and tables. A new family isolates the change from older rooms. Item 1 is the gap: the family reuses a Destination whose publication check doesn't know it. Changes requested, item 1.\n\n## Security\n\nAuthority holds. A citation grants nothing, the new action goes only where the ruling says, and no note can inject markup or borrow an author. Items 2 to 4 aren't access defects. One lets any writer deny the screen to others, one drops evidence of a rollback, and one sends a signed envelope to another origin on a redirect. Changes requested, items 2 to 4.\n\n## Simplification\n\n`commons@1` has no rules at all, and the reference has one shape check. The family adds five pins, which the rulings require. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: changes requested, item 1.\n- Security: changes requested, items 2 to 4.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks:\n  - These hold: the kernel additions, the preserved pins, Membership9's lists, the Rules14 and Directory22 path, creation, the local native 23-note witness, the unplanned configuration and the evidence.\n  - These are needed: items 1 to 5, each with its case, item 6 in the docs, and one full gate at the final head.\n  - Parent 41f77a01 stays open for hosted W1.\n\nA head that makes these changes can come back for a review of its diff from this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d801dca6af3520fdbd1e073acc556e1bb31fe821","binding":"assigned","head":"e272eb7c60fc1f2d70341371d0c08aaa5f732f28","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40b9f933aa4a7b8673cfa75921d3812e380455e1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:614c265aff0dd7168ccc9ba3bce259f795669fcb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:732b482e671ee3710c93867824dac51f36378e3d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0e0540d05529c59477c703b9329d3a8dcb83e8ce, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a31300f9f106a0368df05567e299ebb6f1fa96e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ad1c572d617ee54bbbbeb40e39320b8cfaa47ef, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2354a578b23c36029e5631e8dbf4b0282c21bfd9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31628edb67fee66e7eae5dd63e1a33e510317b48, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33a5bb07c105629339ab1cf5c4e0e392a4985604, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40b9f933aa4a7b8673cfa75921d3812e380455e1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:49d930d1b93c61527cbe2817960f514e98ac3e78, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5acce56bbdb39a21e39463413392dd1f5c615040, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c35be92dfae302e8d18efaa4bb8e56c14225a32, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65a108439882d7737402972fd916fcc4408f6750, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6af57691c267e2ab1a94472db05dd5f2c062fa01, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6d2dcadd4002cc2c9740af8ce581842d57e2ca5b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72bce04e4b0886541e0539a63453276e6692dbd1, git:sha1:589bca98273